    </header><nav class="home-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/websites/">Websites &amp; pricing</a><a href="/local-seo/" aria-current="page">Local SEO</a><a href="/ai-search-visibility/">AI &amp; Search Visibility</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></nav><main id="main"><nav class="breadcrumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span aria-current="page">Local SEO</span></nav><section class="intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Local SEO · Bend & Central Oregon</p><h1>Local SEO &amp; Google Business Profile Help in Bend, Oregon</h1><p class="lede">Help nearby customers find accurate information, understand your services and get in touch.</p></section><section class="section wrap local-layout"><div class="feature-price"><p class="eyebrow">Google Business Profile creation</p><h2>$200 <small>one-time</small></h2><p>Creation assistance for one business profile, with business details, service information and a connection to your website.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=gbp-creation">Start your business profile ↗</a><p class="fine">You keep control of the account. Eligibility and verification follow Google’s process. Ongoing management is separate.</p></div><div><h2>Already have a profile?</h2><p>We can review what you have and quote the improvements you actually need.</p><article class="service-row"><span class="number">01</span><h3>A clear Google presence</h3><p>Review categories, services, hours, contact details and service areas for accuracy.</p></article><article class="service-row"><span class="number">02</span><h3>A useful local website</h3><p>Explain what you do and where you work, with readable mobile pages and an easy way to contact you.</p></article><article class="service-row"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Consistency & honest reviews</h3><p>Align business information across relevant listings and make it easier to request genuine customer feedback.</p></article></div></section><section class="section wrap review-layout"><article class="feature-price review-offer" id="visibility-review"><p class="eyebrow">Search &amp; AI Visibility Review</p><h2>$350 <small>one-time</small></h2><p>Find out what’s missing, what matters and what to fix first.</p><ul><li>Up to 10 website pages</li><li>Discovery, technical and content checks</li><li>5 customer questions sampled across 2 agreed AI services</li><li>A plain-English report with prioritized recommendations</li></ul><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=visibility-review">Ask about a visibility review ↗</a><p class="fine">Assessment only. Implementation is quoted separately. Sources, sample dates, limitations and access requirements are documented.</p></article><div class="review-context"><h2>Not sure where to start?</h2><p>The combined review looks at your website’s search and AI visibility together, so you get one prioritized plan.</p><p>Tell us if local discovery is your main concern. We’ll confirm the review scope and any Business Profile access before work begins.</p><h3>Fixes are scoped separately.</h3><p>Profile cleanup, listing corrections, website improvements and ongoing support are quoted around the agreed work.</p><h3>Measure what matters.</h3><p>Where access and data are available, we review search visibility, profile actions and website inquiries, alongside a record of completed work.</p></div></section><section class="section wrap faq"><div class="section-head"><h2>A few straight answers.</h2></div><details><summary>Why doesn’t my business show up on Google Maps?</summary><p>There can be several reasons: eligibility or verification, inaccurate information, relevance to the search, competition or the searcher’s location. Google describes relevance, distance and prominence as key factors. We review the specifics before recommending a fix; nobody can move your business closer to every searcher.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need a website if I already have a Business Profile?</summary><p>A profile helps people find key details. A website gives you room to explain your services, qualifications, service areas and customer questions. They serve different purposes and should work together.</p></details><details><summary>Can you help with reviews?</summary><p>Yes. We can scope a process for requesting genuine feedback and handling responses. We don’t create fake reviews, filter requests to seek only positive feedback, or guarantee ratings.</p></details><details><summary>Can you guarantee rankings or leads?</summary><p>No. We explain the work, the evidence and the limitations. Search results vary by location and over time. Our goal is a clearer, more useful business presence.</p></details><details><summary>Is local SEO included in website hosting?</summary><p>Profile creation, cleanup and ongoing SEO work are separate. Growth includes a quarterly Search & AI Visibility summary, not a full ongoing SEO service.</p></details></section><p class="wrap source-note">Learn more: <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/7091">Google’s explanation of local rankings ↗</a></p><section class="cta wrap"><div><h2>Let’s find your next step.</h2><p>Tell us about your business and what you need.</p></div><a class="button light" href="/contact/">Let’s talk ↗</a></section></main><footer class="footer">
